Example 3: 
In a playground, 3 brothers and 7 other boys are playing together. How many ways can all the boys be seated in a circular order so that none of the three brothers are seated together? 
Solution: 
The number of ways to arrange 11 boys in a circular manner without restriction is; 
(10-1)! = 9! 
The number of ways to arrange the boys where the 3 brothers are seated beside each other is;  
7P7 (other boys) • 3P3 (3 brothers) 
Hence, the numbers of ways to arrange if none of the 3 brothers are seated together are; 
9! - ( 7P7 • 3P3) 
362,880 - 30,240 = 332,640 ways
